{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-K-flat-resolution}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:15c9b9d863511f8c3ea216bb2bca7c06164084c2ac46e94d6f7acf8dc1ef2cc9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a28b7f0f12e6ca00718ee2c2ab9002bf61f925ec49d73f5c394520aa975f8d00", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. For any complex\n<MATH_0002> there exists a <MATH_0003>-flat complex <MATH_0004>\nwhose terms are flat <MATH_0005>-modules and a quasi-isomorphism\n<MATH_0006> which is termwise surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1cd54dc4512b8e9b61e538c628244851e6dd22b6f4e7f96c104f4190cd7e5df2", "unit_id": "tag:06YS:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet$", "MATH_0004": "$\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\colim \\mathcal{K}_n^m$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-resolution-by-direct-sums-extensions-by-zero}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-j-shriek-flat}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-bounded-flat-K-flat}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-colimit-K-flat}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-resolution-by-direct-sums-extensions-by-zero}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3d9d801339635b0457e022e8b9a9fa66d09dba2ed097b8f056931d950f155d79", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:80c039395daae1f7132f07bbfe582620f028030c38e2fccf393c1b60cd55f1f9", "source_text": "Choose a diagram as in\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nEach complex <MATH_0001> is a bounded\nabove complex of flat modules, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nHence <MATH_0002> is K-flat by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nThus <MATH_0003> is K-flat by\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nThe induced map\n<MATH_0004>\nis a quasi-isomorphism and termwise surjective by construction.\nProperty (3) of Lemma <REF_0005>\nshows that <MATH_0005> is a direct sum of\nflat modules and hence flat which proves the final assertion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a0716c4464fa65500bd7100f14966f2c8feec0a14ac0dac40b14e3e72ad3ed5", "unit_id": "tag:06YS:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\alpha : \\mathcal{P}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\text{Tot}(\\text{id}_{\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet} \\otimes \\alpha) :\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{P}^\\bullet)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet)\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-derived-tor-quasi-isomorphism-other-side}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a05130c1871610722cee6c9a22771a4576b5a5c98e7f1f96ca55daef785cca3e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f95894aad2cd55dc9a2c5c898fa9482e0f8175fe08ec642bf2ae0138fa8e3fe", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site. Let\n<MATH_0002> be a\nquasi-isomorphism of K-flat complexes of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nFor every complex <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>-modules\nthe induced map\n<MATH_0006>\nis a quasi-isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a84860b5b58c31e0639ae9ff0010438ac1bbab993eb8951e24b9ab01b1b8330", "unit_id": "tag:06YT:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet\n\\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{P}^\\bullet) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet\n\\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet\n\\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{P}^\\bullet) \\ar[r] &\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet\n\\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{Q}^\\bullet)\n}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-resolution}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-quasi-isomorphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:976c1978b95a0e1107a4c93f40ee654ec2e800f79f6fff0f7630d5f4f9074a24", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53d5f34cc3b7593987df3d6f97d4aa5796fa2d4b5722a87c699c134dbbb597fa", "source_text": "Choose a quasi-isomorphism <MATH_0001>\nwith <MATH_0002> a K-flat complex, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nConsider the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0003>\nThe result follows as by\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthe vertical arrows and the top horizontal arrow are quasi-isomorphisms.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:81bee15f7578028415b3fac4133d741109c9adc7952e03ac461d9b700e39246e", "unit_id": "tag:06YT:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet \\to \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nK(\\mathcal{O})\n\\longrightarrow\nK(\\mathcal{O}),\n\\quad\n\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet\n\\longmapsto\n\\text{Tot}(\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O} \\mathcal{K}^\\bullet)\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$D(\\mathcal{O}) \\to D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0007": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0008": "$K(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0009": "$K$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{K}^\\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-resolution}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-derived-tor-exact}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-K-flat-quasi-isomorphism}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-derived-tor-quasi-isomorphism-other-side}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:05829885dbb3961fff37c13163847d4ab5c0c56c86d81493afbb42a3658a18cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:efa92bdf2212ace0fe15714810df2c003e6f75a9e56f0589a0c14bdef348cad6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nChoose a K-flat resolution <MATH_0004>, see\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0002>\nwe obtain an exact functor of triangulated categories\n<MATH_0005>\nBy\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthis functor induces a functor\n<MATH_0006> simply because\n<MATH_0007> is the localization of <MATH_0008>\nat quasi-isomorphisms.\nAs the category of <MATH_0009>-flat resolutions of <MATH_0010> is\ncofiltered and as we have\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthe resulting functor (up to isomorphism)\ndoes not depend on the choice of <MATH_0011>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c62fbf140c92e0c0f1d47cd2f9f06abd34fd56e7880669b657831e9d3a56e113", "unit_id": "tag:06YL:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n- \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet :\nD(\\mathcal{O})\n\\longrightarrow\nD(\\mathcal{O})\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-derived-tor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3c5dd7b4c3a68777de4825f18dccde73b0ed01d9090c9a9ff3f4d941a9940df1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6d3262ea78766b4659904cd4a26d28f449784dcc06cb40225acbf9053cc3e19c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an object of <MATH_0003>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>derived tensor product<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0004>\nis the exact functor of triangulated categories described above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:276891f26546a73d33d39e4227f051f56e8d1ca460dbe3430119ff984868cbcd", "unit_id": "tag:06YU:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet\n\\cong\n\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{F}^\\bullet\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0004": "$D(\\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}^\\bullet \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^{\\mathbf{L}} \\mathcal{G}^\\bullet$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-section-sign-rules}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ffdf98e57fd0540661e490f28588ece9f2c255bfd427085a5e797725756fd716", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a4d9213d30a720034a6e9aa7fc4814ecd73ed6b7eb59d11aaa4922723aa283d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt is clear from our explicit constructions that\nthere is a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0001>\nfor <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> in <MATH_0004>.\nHere we use sign rules as given in More on Algebra, Section\n<REF_0001>. Hence when we write\n<MATH_0005>\nwe will usually be agnostic about which variable we are using to\ndefine the derived tensor product with.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9d48b14d52ca9fef3258245a0c7116e649b6ce31e74443593f498b753a6e52f2", "unit_id": "tag:06YL:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06YL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\text{Tor}_p^\\mathcal{O}(\\mathcal{F}, \\mathcal{G}) =\nH^{-p}(\\mathcal{F} \\otimes_\\mathcal{O}^\\mathbf{L} \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-tor}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b9748d087b54b614957c356e94b1379d0b175d4fec44d4c8909d22b2ee68beeb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:569fb855b28a7df01c5aafec5bcf5fccf983945562a5f7325567c1d1db665c50", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nLet <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> be <MATH_0004>-modules.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>Tor<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>'s of <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are defined by\nthe formula\n<MATH_0007>\nwith derived tensor product as defined above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fbabd59f44609041c3b319a506984cca76604b6e969a385cb642d75401d78a49", "unit_id": "tag:08FF:statement"}
